  "body": "**What changed**\r\n\r\n- The Machine page's \"Library\" list reads the Machines pane's catalogue\r\n  (`machines_pane::refresh`). It shows the machines in the user machines folder first, then\r\n  a separator, then the shipped machines.\r\n- A user machine shows `name (file name)`. A refused file adds `- refused: <first refusal>`,\r\n  and its row is disabled.\r\n- A file selection queues `UseCatalogueMachine(MachineSource::File(..))`. A shipped\r\n  selection still queues `LoadBuiltinMachine`. No command or project field is new.\r\n- When the setup uses a file, the combo shows the file's label, not \"other\".\r\n- When the list opens, the page reads the folder again.\r\n- \"Load other\" opens in the user machines folder when the folder exists\r\n  (`machines_pane::dialog_start`).\r\n- `ShellUi::blank` sets no user machines folder. Thus no UI test reads the real folder of\r\n  the tester.\r\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2358-setup-user-machines.md`.\r\n\r\n**Readings**\r\n\r\nBranched from `main` at `94f7d6b89`.\r\n\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 16 steps (`ui suites: lib` 1043\r\n  passed).\r\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --base upstream/main`: green. The first run stopped at step 786\r\n  because of a local time limit. The 36 remaining steps (the last app suites, all ui\r\n  suites, `clippy -D warnings`) then ran with `--only` and passed.\r\n- Seen in the desktop app on Windows: a user machine is at the top of the list, it mounts,\r\n  undo restores the previous machine, and \"Load other\" opens in\r\n  `%APPDATA%\\camcraft\\machines`.\r\n\r\n**Pinning tests** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_user_machines.rs`)\r\n\r\n- `the_library_lists_the_user_machines_first`\r\n- `picking_a_user_machine_mounts_it_and_undo_restores_the_last`\r\n- `a_refused_user_machine_is_listed_with_its_reason_and_cannot_be_picked`\r\n- `load_other_starts_in_the_user_machines_folder_when_it_exists`\r\n\r\n**Not exercised**\r\n\r\n- The browser build. It has no user machines folder, so its list does not change.\r\n- macOS and Linux. The folder lookup (`store::user_dir`) did not change.\r\n- The real file dialog in a test. The test checks `dialog_start` only, because the rfd\r\n  modal cannot run in the harness.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The Setup page's machine Library list shows your own machines first, then the shipped ones; \"Load other\" opens in your user machines folder (#2358)\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nFixes #2358 ",
